{
  "id": "ch5",
  "title": "THE OBSERVATORY",
  "objPage": "S7A1",
  "preset": "coldlab",
  "notes": [
    "COHERENCE (2026-10-22): ch5 climbs to Echo's observatory and goes inside, one way: a0 THE CLIFF ROAD is the rock road up the cliff at night (E5a0 1696-2464 only), a1 THE COPIED VAULT is the observatory's library and instrument halls (E7a2 448-1472 only: shelves, chart rolls, the dark stacks), a2 is the dome itself (E7a3 0-1264 only): the vat hall under the ribbed dome (the tunnel ribs), the broadcast room (the consoles) and the dish gallery where Echo fights. Each area walks back and forth through its one source strip (legs <= 512 px, leftward legs mirrored), so every join is a mirror join or a continuation; the place changes only at the fades.",
    "Palette: night (scale + 15% toward #2a3a6a) on the cliff; inside, one cold blue-violet light for the halls and the dome (saturation 0.75, lightness 0.92, 22% toward #4a5aa0; the tanks 12%), so the library and the dome read as one building at night. The cliff's far layer is E5a0's mountains under the night sky; the library and the dome have no far layer (their open stacks and openings show the dark backdrop).",
    "5-4 THE VAT HALL keeps Echo's clean tank row: E8a0 592-1104 tanks 05-08 (h 112-240, blend over the dome ribs) at area x 0, so game.js HERO_TANKS (x 30, 175, 320, 464) stand in their glass; 5-6 carries tanks 07-08 again (E8a0 864-1120 at x 2048: HERO_TANKS x 2096, 2240).",
    "Boss arena (5-6, DR. ECHO with the acoustic dish): the dish gallery under the dome ribs, the broadcast consoles and their screens (Echo's command transmitter) on both sides of the lock (E7a3 880-1264, before the original COMPUTER ROOM boss window at 1264); the runtime adds the vat vents."
